          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong connection
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            – a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            or an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            – is a rule that identifies
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p There are several different but equivalent formalizations of this idea:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                as a
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
                functor,
            %li
              %p
                as a rule for a
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant derivative
            %li
              %p
                as a
                %strong distribution (field) of horizontal subspaces
                – an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
                – and via a
                %strong
                  connection
                  = succeed "-form" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                which annihilates the distribution of horizontal subspaces. The connection in that sense induces a smooth version of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+connection"} Hurewicz connection
          %p
            The usual textbook convention is to say just connection for the distribution of horizontal subspaces, and the objects of the other three approaches one calls more specifically covariant derivative, connection
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
          %p In the remainder of this Idea-section we discuss a bit more how to understand connections in terms of parallel transport.
          %p
            Given a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %em connection
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a prescription to associate with each path
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\gamma : x \to y
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} path groupoid
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}_1(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra(\gamma)
            between the fibers of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            over these points
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi tra
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi γ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi γ
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P_x &amp;\stackrel{tra(\gamma)}{\to}&amp; P_y
                  \\\
                  x &amp;\stackrel{\gamma}{\to}&amp; y
                  }
          %p such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                this assignment respects the structure on the fibers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_x
                (for instance is
                = succeed "-equivariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                is a
                = succeed "-bundle" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                is a vector bundle);
            %li
              %p this assignment is smooth in a suitable sense;
            %li
              %p
                this assignment is
                = succeed "ial" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi γ
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \stackrel{\gamma}{\to} y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi γ
                          %mo ′
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \stackrel{\gamma'}{\to} z
                of composable paths in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                we have
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi P
                                %mi x
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi tra
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi P
                                %mi y
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi tra
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi P
                                %mi z
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi x
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi γ
                            %mtd
                              %mi y
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo ′
                            %mtd
                              %mi z
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi P
                                %mi x
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi tra
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi P
                                %mi z
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi x
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi γ
                            %mtd
                              %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      P_x &amp;\stackrel{tra(\gamma)}{\to}&amp; P_y &amp;\stackrel{tra(\gamma')}{\to}&amp; P_z
                      \\\
                      x &amp;\stackrel{\gamma}{\to}&amp; y &amp;\stackrel{\gamma'}{\to}&amp; z
                      }
                      \\;\;\;
                      \=
                      \\;\;\;
                      \\array{
                      P_x &amp;\stackrel{tra(\gamma' \circ \gamma)}{\to}&amp; P_z
                      \\\
                      x &amp;\stackrel{\gamma'\circ \gamma}{\to}&amp; z
                      }
          %p
            In other words, a connection on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi At
                  %mo ″
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tra : \mathbf{P}_1(X) \to At''(P)
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} path groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+groupoid"} Atiyah Lie groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            that is smooth in a suitable sense and
            %em splits the Atiyah sequence
            in that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi tra
                  %mi At
                  %mo ″
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}_1(X) \stackrel{tra}{\to} At''(X) \to \mathbf{P}_1(X)
            (see the notation at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+groupoid"} Atiyah Lie groupoid
          %p
            %strong Terminology
          %p
            The functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra
            is called the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            of the connection. This terminology comes from looking at the orbits of all points in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra
            (i.e. from looking at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of
            = succeed "):" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi tra
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            sitting over paths in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and one thinks of the image of a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P_x
            under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra(\gamma)
            as the result of propagating
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            parallel to these curves in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %p
            %strong Flat connections
          %p
            It may happen that the assignment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                  %mo :
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi tra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra : \gamma \mapsto tra(\gamma)
            only depends on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            class of the path
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            relative to its endpoints
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra
            factors through the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1(X) \to \Pi_1(X)
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} path groupoid
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
          %h3#more_concrete_picture More concrete picture
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie differentiation
            the functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi tra
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+groupoid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi at
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla : T X \to at(P)
          %p
            of vector bundles. Locally on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – meaning: when everything is pulled back to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – this is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lie(G)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form#twisted"} valued
            1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
