          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connections"} Ehresmann connections
            originates with:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Les connexions infinitésimales dans un espace fibré différentiable
              %p Colloque de topologie (espaces fibrés), Bruxelles, 1950, Georges Thone, Liège; Masson et Cie., Paris (1951) 29–55
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S%C3%A9minaire+Bourbaki"}> Séminaire Bourbaki
                ,
                %strong 1
                24 (1952) 153–168 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1948-1951__1__153_0"}> numdam:SB_1948-1951__1__153_0
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/SB_1948-1951__1__153_0.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The understanding of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potentials"} gauge potentials
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            originates with (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
          %ul
            %li#WuYang75
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tai+Tsun+Wu"}> Tai Tsun Wu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chen+Ning+Yang"} Chen Ning Yang
              = succeed "," do
                %em Concept of nonintegrable phase factors and global formulation of gauge fields
              %strong 12
              (1975) 3845 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.12.3845"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.12.3845
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Werner+Greub"}> Werner Greub
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Halperin"} Stephen Halperin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ray+Vanstone"} Ray Vanstone
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Connections%2C+Curvature%2C+and+Cohomology"} Connections, Curvature, and Cohomology
              Academic Press (1973)
          %p
            With an eye towards application in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tohru+Eguchi"}> Tohru Eguchi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Gilkey"} Peter Gilkey
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Hanson"} Andrew Hanson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravitation, gauge theories and differential geometry
                %strong 66
                6 (1980) 213-393 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(80)90130-1"}> doi:10.1016/0370-1573(80)90130-1
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikio+Nakahara"}> Mikio Nakahara
                , Chapter 9 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometry%2C+Topology+and+Physics"} Geometry, Topology and Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781315275826"} doi:10.1201/9781315275826
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://alpha.sinp.msu.ru/~panov/LibBooks/GRAV/(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)Mikio_Nakahara-Geometry,_Topology_and_Physics,_Second_Edition_(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)-Institute_of_Physics_Publishing(2003).pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerd+Rudolph"}> Gerd Rudolph
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Schmidt"} Matthias Schmidt
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Geometry and Mathematical Physics Part II. Fibre Bundles, Topology and Gauge Fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-024-0959-8"} doi:10.1007/978-94-024-0959-8
          %p
            The formulation of connections in terms of their smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            is in
          %ul
            %li#SchreiberWaldorf07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              = succeed "," do
                %em Parallel Transport and Functors
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0452"} arXiv:0705.0452
          %p based on a series of classical observations. I farily comprehensive commented list of related references is here:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#HistConnAsParTrans"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos – References – Connections – In terms of parallel transport
          %p Basic facts about connections, such as the existence proof in terms of Cech cocycles, are collected in the brief lecture note
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Voronov"}> Theodore Voronov
              ,
              %em Differential Geometry, §3 Connection on a vector bundle
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.manchester.ac.uk/~tv/Teaching/Differential%20Geometry/2008-2009/lecture3.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Discussion of connection form (mostly on trivial bundles) in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            includes the following
          %ul
            %li#Kock06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Connections and path connections in groupoids
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.au.dk/publs?publid=619"} web
            %li#Kock07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Group valued differential forms revisited
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.au.dk/publs?publid=636"} web
